      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 3. Powers and Duties. (a) The Deputy Commissioner shall receive and investigate complaints from any source or upon his own initiative or at the direction of the Commissioner of Investigation regarding alleged acts of corruption or other criminal activity, conflicts of interest, unethical conduct, and misconduct within the City School District of the City of New York, including the Board of Education, the Office of the Chancellor and the Community School Boards. The Deputy Commissioner may refer such matters involving unethical conduct or misconduct as he or she deems appropriate to the Board of Education, the Chancellor, a Community School Board, or Community Superintendent, as appropriate, for",
